-- title:
--   Twisted Eisenstein term: slope, Eisenstein-table atoms, atom-free remainder
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $L/K$ is a Galois extension of number fields, $\mathbb A=\mathbb A_L$ denotes the adele ring of $L$, $\|x\|=\mathrm{ideleNorm}_L(x)$ denotes the module of an idele (the real value of `distribHaarChar` on $\mathbb A^\times$), and finite places of $L$ are written $\mathfrak w$, the letter $w$ being reserved for the real exponent occurring below. Set $\mathcal S=\{g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A):\|\det g\|\in[\alpha,\beta]\}$, the *slab* cut out by two reals $0<\alpha<\beta$.
--
--   **Geometric data.** A set $\Phi_L\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A)$ contained in $\mathcal S$ which is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under `globalPoints` acting on the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` restricted to $\mathcal S$; a Borel-measurable structure on $\mathbb A^\times$, a Haar measure $\nu_{Z}$ on $\mathbb A^\times$ and a fundamental domain $\Omega_L$ for the principal ideles (the range of $L^\times\to\mathbb A^\times$) with respect to $\nu_Z$; reals $c,u,d_1,d_2$ with $c>0$, a compact set $T_c$ and a second set $\Phi_0$ which is contained in $\bigcup_{y\in T_c}(\,\cdot\,y)$-translates of the centre-cut Siegel set `centreCutSiegelSet L c u d₁ d₂` (integral finite part; local height $\ge c$ at every infinite place; window square $\le u^2$; archimedean determinant norms in $[d_1,d_2]$), is contained in $\mathcal S$, and is again a fundamental domain for $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ on the restricted Haar measure.
--
--   **Galois data.** An idele Galois descent datum $D$ for $L/K$, that is a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)\to\mathrm{RingAut}(\mathbb A)$ compatible with $\mathrm{algebraMap}$ on $L$ and continuous in each argument, together with $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every $\tau$ lies in `Subgroup.zpowers σ` (so the group is generated by $\sigma$).
--
--   **Character and level data.** A finite set $S_L$ of finite places of $L$ which is saturated over $K$ (`hSL`: $\mathfrak w\in S_L\iff\mathfrak w'\in S_L$ whenever $\mathfrak w,\mathfrak w'$ lie under the same place of $K$); a homomorphism $\xi_L$ from the top subgroup of $\mathbb A^\times$ to $\mathbb C^\times$ which is continuous (`hξc`), trivial on the principal ideles (`hξt`), and of modulus $\|\xi_L(z)\|=\|z\|^{w}$ for a fixed real $w$ (`hξw`); an ideal $N$ of $\mathcal O_L$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_L$ (`hN`); and a homomorphism $\xi'$ with $\xi'(z)=\xi_L(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}(\sigma)z)$, i.e. the $\sigma$-translate of $\xi_L$ (`hξ'`).
--
--   **Test-function data.** An archimedean type family $\mathrm{tys}_L$ (a finite family of archimedean representations at each infinite place of $L$), a finite set $S$ of finite places of $K$, a function $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles, and semi-local factors $\varphi_S(v)$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ for each finite place $v$ of $K$.
--
--   **Tables.** A set $X$ of tables $x:\{\text{finite places of }L\}\to\mathbb C\times\mathbb C$ which, by `hX`, contains every table $x$ such that $x_{\mathfrak w}=0$ for $\mathfrak w\in S_L$ and, for $\mathfrak w\notin S_L$, $(x_{\mathfrak w})_2=c_{\mathfrak w}\,\xi_L(\det\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\mathfrak w)$ with $c_{\mathfrak w}=\mathrm{cNorm}(\mathfrak w)=N(\mathfrak w)$, $\|(x_{\mathfrak w})_1\|\le (N(\mathfrak w)+1)\sqrt{\|\xi_L(\det\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\mathfrak w)\|}$, and $\overline{(x_{\mathfrak w})_1}=\overline{(x_{\mathfrak w})_2}\,\|(x_{\mathfrak w})_2\|^{-1}(x_{\mathfrak w})_1$.
--
--   Let $\alpha_m:\mathbb A^\times\to\mathbb R^\times$ be the homomorphism induced by the module $\|\cdot\|$, and let the adeles carry their Borel structure. The remaining data are quantified inside the statement: positivity `hαm` of the values of $\alpha_m$; a countable index type $\iota_E$; families of characters $\mu_E,\nu_E:\iota_E\to\mathrm{Hom}(\mathbb A^\times,\mathbb C^\times)$ subject to the group of hypotheses `_hμ`–`_hdist`, namely that each $\mu_E(e),\nu_E(e)$ is unitary (modulus $1$ everywhere), trivial on principal ideles, continuous, that $\mu_E(e)(z)\nu_E(e)(z)\|z\|^{w}=\xi'(z)$ for all $z$, and that distinct indices are separated by some norm-one idele; integers $n_E(e)$ and sections $\varphi_E(e,j,s,\cdot)$ subject to the group `_hφE`–`_hφEty`, namely that each $\varphi_E(e,j,s)$ is an induced section for the pair $(\mu_E(e)\|\cdot\|^{s+1/2},\ \nu_E(e)\|\cdot\|^{-(s+1/2)})$ (transforming under the adelic Borel subgroup by the product of these characters evaluated on the two diagonal entries), is archimedean $K$-finite, $K_f$-smooth, jointly continuous in $(s,g)$, entire in $s$ for each $g$, has its right translates under each archimedean row-isometry subgroup contained in a fixed finite-dimensional space, is flat on the adelic maximal compact subgroup (its value there is that at $s=0$), is right invariant under `principalLevel (𝓞 L) L N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L`, and lies in the type-cut submodule `archCutSubmodule L tysL`; the orthonormality hypothesis `_hφEon`, that $\int \varphi_E(e,i,0)\overline{\varphi_E(e,j,0)}$ over the maximal compact with `maximalCompactHaar` is $\delta_{ij}$; the completeness hypotheses `_hφEspan` and `_hpairs`, the first asserting that on the unitary axis $s=it$ every induced section for $(\mu_E(e),\nu_E(e))$ with the same continuity, $K$-finiteness, level-$N$ invariance and type properties lies in the span of the $\varphi_E(e,j,it)$, the second that every unitary, idele-class, continuous pair $(\mu',\nu')$ with $\mu'\nu'\|\cdot\|^{w}=\xi'$ carrying a non-zero such section is matched on the norm-one ideles by some index $e$; and continuation data: sets $O_E(e,j)\subseteq\mathbb C$ and functions $E_E(e,j,s,\cdot)$, $N_E(e,j,s,\cdot)$ subject to `_hEE` (eight clauses), which require $O_E(e,j)$ to be open, preconnected and to contain both the imaginary axis $\{\mathrm{Re}\,s=0\}$ and the half-plane $\{\mathrm{Re}\,s>1/2\}$, the functions $s\mapsto E_E(e,j,s,g)$ and $s\mapsto N_E(e,j,s,g)$ to be analytic on a neighbourhood of $O_E(e,j)$ for each $g$ with joint continuity on $O_E(e,j)\times\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A)$, and, for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>1/2$, $E_E(e,j,s,g)=\varphi_E(e,j,s,g)+\sum_{\xi\in L}\varphi_E\bigl(e,j,s,\,\mathrm{adelicWeyl}\cdot u(\xi)\cdot g\bigr)$ and $N_E(e,j,s,g)=\int_{\mathbb A}\varphi_E(e,j,s,\mathrm{adelicWeyl}^{-1}u(x)g)\,dx$ with respect to the adelic additive Haar measure; finally a real number $\kappa$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a sequence of tables $\mathrm{tabs}:\mathbb N\to(\{\text{finite places of }L\}\to\mathbb C\times\mathbb C)$ with $\mathrm{tabs}(n)\in X$ for all $n$, and coefficients $c:\mathbb N\to\mathbb C$, such that:
--
--   1.
--
--   $\sum_n\|c_n\|<\infty$;
--
--   2.
--
--   for every $n$ with $c_n\neq0$: the table $\mathrm{tabs}(n)$ is constant on fibres outside $S_L$ (if $\mathfrak w,\mathfrak w'\notin S_L$ lie under the same place of $K$ then $\mathrm{tabs}(n)_{\mathfrak w}=\mathrm{tabs}(n)_{\mathfrak w'}$), and there are a non-zero ideal $M$ of $\mathcal O_L$ and two continuous homomorphisms $\chi_1,\chi_2:\mathbb A^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$, each trivial on the principal ideles, with $\mathrm{tabs}(n)_{\mathfrak w}=\bigl(a_{\mathfrak w},b_{\mathfrak w}\bigr)$ for all $\mathfrak w\notin S_L$, where $(a,b)$ is the Hecke eigensystem [`LanglandsTunnell.Converse.eisensteinTableOf L M hM χ₁ χ₂`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ConverseData.html#L132), that is $a_{\mathfrak w}=\chi_1(\pi_{\mathfrak w})+\chi_2(\pi_{\mathfrak w})$ and $b_{\mathfrak w}=\chi_1(\pi_{\mathfrak w})\chi_2(\pi_{\mathfrak w})$ with $\pi_{\mathfrak w}$ the uniformiser idele at $\mathfrak w$;
--
--   3.
--
--   and for every finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ disjoint from $S$ with $\#T\ge2$, no place of $L$ above a $v\in T$ lying in $S_L$, every choice of an extension $\mathrm{ws}(v)$ of each $v$ to $L$, every map $w'$ with $(w'(v))^{\mathrm{asIdeal}}=\sigma^{-1}\!\cdot(\mathrm{ws}(v))^{\mathrm{asIdeal}}$ for $v\in T$, every family $\varpi_v$ in the completed valuation rings at $\mathrm{ws}(v)$ which is irreducible and of non-zero image for $v\in T$, every family $r_T(v):\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{\mathrm{ws}(v)})$ forming a Hecke coset system for the integral subgroup and the element $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1)$ at each $v\in T$, and every family $z_v$ with $z_v=\varpi_v\cdot 1$ (the central matrix) for $v\in T$, there exist continuous linear functionals $\mu,\nu:C(X,\mathbb C)\to\mathbb C$ with the following two properties.
--
--   (i) *(Atom-freeness of $\mu$ in the $T$-coordinates.)* For every $\tau:\{\text{finite places of }K\}\to\mathbb C\times\mathbb C$ and every $\varepsilon>0$ there are sets $U_v\subseteq\mathbb C\times\mathbb C$ such that $U_v$ is open and contains $\tau_v$ for each $v\in T$, and such that $\|\mu(g)\|<\varepsilon$ for every $g\in C(X,\mathbb C)$ with $\|g\|\le1$ pointwise which vanishes at every table $y\in X$ for which $y_{w'(v)}\notin U_v$ for some $v\in T$.
--
--   (ii) For all exponent functions $k,j:\{\text{finite places of }K\}\to\mathbb N$, every continuous compactly supported $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A)$ and every $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles such that `IsSemiLocalFactorization K L (S ∪ T) φ φa φf` holds for the semi-local factors given at $v\in T$ by $x\mapsto\sum_{\iota:\mathrm{Fin}(k_v)\to\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)}\mathbf 1_{\mathcal I_v}\bigl(\mathrm{semiLocalComponent}(\mathrm{localEmbed}(\prod_m r_T(v)(\iota_m)\cdot z_v^{\,j_v}))^{-1}x\bigr)$ and by $\varphi_S(v)$ otherwise (the predicate requires $\varphi_a$ to be an archimedean test factor, $\varphi_f$ a locally constant compactly supported finite test factor, each listed semi-local factor a semi-local test function, $\varphi_f(h)$ to equal the product of the semi-local factors when all components off $S\cup T$ are integral and to vanish otherwise, and $\varphi(g)=\varphi_a(\mathrm{arch}\,g)\varphi_f(\mathrm{fin}\,g)$), with $\varphi$ bi-invariant under $\mathrm{levelOne}(N)\cap\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles and archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$ (that is, $g\mapsto\varphi(g^{-1})$ lies in `archCutSubmodule L tysL` and $\varphi$ in the corresponding dual cut submodule): for every $g\in C(X,\mathbb C)$ given by $$g(x)=\prod_{v\in T}\bigl((x_{w'(v)})_1\bigr)^{k_v}\Bigl(c_{w'(v)}^{-1}(x_{w'(v)})_2\Bigr)^{j_v},$$ and every function $I:\mathbb R\to\mathbb C$ and real $R_2$ such that for all $R\ge R_2$ $$I(R)=\kappa\sum_{e\in\iota_E}\int_{\mathbb R}\sum_{i,j<n_E(e)}\Bigl(\int_{K_{\max}}\bigl(\varphi_E(e,j,it)\,\|\det\|^{w/2}\bigr)\!*\!\varphi\,(k)\ \overline{\varphi_E(e,i,it)(k)}\,dk\Bigr)\Bigl(\int_{\Phi_0}\Lambda^{e^{R}}E_E(e,i,it)(x)\ \overline{\Lambda^{e^{R}}\bigl(E_E(e,j,it)\circ\sigma_{\mathbb A}^{-1}\bigr)(x)}\,dx\Bigr)dt,$$ where the first inner integral is over the adelic maximal compact subgroup with `maximalCompactHaar` and the convolution is `rightConv`, $\sigma_{\mathbb A}^{-1}$ is `sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`, the outer $x$-integral is against `adelicGLHaar`, and $\Lambda^{e^{R}}$ is the truncation operator `lambdaT` at height $e^{R}$ for the adelic height of $L$, the unipotent family $t\mapsto u(t)$ and the measure supplied by `productionPinsOf L ΦL …` (the additive adelic Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box) — one has that $n\mapsto c_n\,g(\mathrm{tabs}(n))$ is summable and $$I(R)-\bigl(R\,\nu(g)+\textstyle\sum_n c_n\,g(\mathrm{tabs}(n))+\mu(g)\bigr)\longrightarrow 0\qquad(R\to+\infty).$$
--
--   This is the evaluation of the continuous-spectrum contribution to the spectral side of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $L$: along Hecke words at a finite set $T$ of places of $K$, the truncated Gram expansion of twisted Eisenstein inner products grows linearly in the truncation parameter $R$, with a linear coefficient $\nu$, an absolutely convergent atomic part whose atoms are Eisenstein Hecke tables $(\chi_1(\pi)+\chi_2(\pi),\chi_1(\pi)\chi_2(\pi))$ that are constant on fibres over $K$, and a remainder functional $\mu$ carrying no mass concentrated at any prescribed point of the $T$-coordinates. It feeds the assembly of the twisted trace formula in [`AutomorphicForm.exists_atomic_forall_tendsto_setIntegral_lambdaT_finsum_integral_sigmaAdelicAct_sub_lambdaT_tsum_finsum_twistedConvOp_sub_lambdaT_finsum_twistedConvOp_chiDet_sub`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_atomic_forall_tendsto_setIntegral_lambdaT_finsum_integral_sigmaAdelicAct_sub_lambdaT_tsum_finsum_twistedConvOp_sub_lambdaT_finsum_twistedConvOp_chiDet_sub).
